WEBVTT

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:09.680
Federation Era, A890303

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.720
The VF376 unmanned observation
satellite detected a spatial warp

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:17.480
in the vicinity of the asteroid
belt in the Lyra constellation.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.780
Following that, a warp of an unknown
celestial body has been confirmed

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.500
In order to observe the body enveloped
in Miguel Storm exceeding level 5,

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.760
an independent mining company was
contracted through a dummy company.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.240
Same day, 0321 - Excavation at
the new celestial body starts.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.880
Orichalt is removed from the rock shell.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:45.280
Same day, 0322 - Planetary Federation's 8th
reconnaissance-in-force fleet's ship Marito

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.200
detains the mining company's vessel.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:54.940
The amount of Orichalt ore extracted was 1437 Tylers, which is much lower than the estimated deposits.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:59.780
At the same time, to evade a group of rocks that performed a spatial warp,

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:02.330
the Marito executed an emergency Miguel jump.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.100
Inside the specific topological dimension used for warping, usually called the Miguel Line,

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.130
the mining company's vessel
performed a forced Miguel Out.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:12.880
Marito lost sight of the target.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:15.310
At the present moment, no
further info is available.

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:26.100
So basically, the mining company got greedy and made off with the Orichalt, then?

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:30.360
While the possibility of that is high,
there's something suspicious about this.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.270
If the Orichalt Marito recovered was,

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:37.700
in fact, all that was inside that new object...

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:43.500
The mining company discovered
something else than Orichalt there?

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:47.630
Also, the group of rocks that
somehow Miguel Jumped.

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:51.380
It has to do something with
Amatsu Mikaboshi, hasn't it?

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:38.540
Deploying shields.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:46.600
Shields deployed.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.860
Entering a meteoroid cloud.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:56.020
Girlie, did you find out our current location?

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:58.460
Yes, I performed some analysis.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:03:59.880
Well, go on.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.880
Our current location is

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.620
in the N-space somewhere around here.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:05.760
N-space?!

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:08.820
That's the undeveloped space
outside the Miguel Net!

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.060
I know we performed a forced Miguel Out,

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:12.940
but it didn't have to throw us out
in such boonies...

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.580
What a pain.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:17.600
Maya, are you sure this isn't a mistake?

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.820
That's what I determined based
on Vega's coordinates.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:23.000
I'm surprised too, you know.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:26.440
Claire, ready the Orichalt torpedo
for jumping for launch.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:26.840
Okay!

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:29.480
We can't stay in this unmapped
place forever, right?

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:32.220
Girlie, pick us a route through the phase space.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:47.220
Sorry, I've got no time for games.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.500
I'm busy with a lot of stuff.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.160
Wait, you understand words?

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:58.940
Don't cry, okay?

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.700
Orichalt torpedo, preparing for launch.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:04.180
Quadrant input finished.

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:06.300
Spacial telemetry connected.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.200
Alright, launch!

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:08.740
Okay.

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:14.540
Time until torpedo reaches the
B point is 7 hours 27 minutes.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:19.060
You hear that?

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:21.540
7 hours and 27 minutes until we jump.

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:25.140
Isn't the B point still outside the net?

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:26.700
It's barely been a day.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.900
If we mess up, we'll fall right
into the military's lap.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:35.320
A detour through some remote area and re-entering
the Miguel Net would take two months at best.

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:36.840
Seriously?

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:39.980
But you can't get any info outside it!

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:44.640
No news! No movies!
No results of asteroid speed races!

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:47.560
Isn't this a good opportunity to rethink your life?

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:50.040
No thanks, I'm good being the
way I am right now.

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:53.420
Hey, I'm going to be hearing the
soldier lady out now.

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:54.380
What are you guys going to do?

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:55.660
That hottie?

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.120
I'm going, going, I'm on my way!

00:05:58.300 --> 00:05:59.420
I agree,

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:02.580
I really want to know the
reason they went after us.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:03.220
Yeah.

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:07.240
In that case, everyone except girlie gather
in the expanded space in 10 minutes.

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:08.320
Got it!
Alright!
Sure!

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:20.440
I-I'm sorry.

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:27.400
Um...

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:28.160
What is it?

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:32.660
The captain said he wants you to
come to the expanded space.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:33.900
Can I refuse?

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:36.580
I don't think so, sorry.

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:43.200
You're the one who retrieved my body, right?

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.780
Yes, it was me.

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:45.560
Why?

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:48.340
What do you mean, why?

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:51.540
Does there need to be a reason
to save someone?

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:54.180
But it was really fortunate, right?

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.920
The fact the MT system happened to be inside the Miguel Cube-

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:58.420
By my superiors.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:00.540
They probably thought it was dangerous.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.240
I-is that so...

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.120
Maya.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:03.840
Yes?

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.280
Are you really a serious criminal?

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:07.500
Those are false accusations!

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:08.760
I'm innocent!

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:15.200
Once you're done, I'll come and take those off.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:16.440
Sure.

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:18.240
That'll be helpful...

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:20.000
In many ways...

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:35.880
What is this place?

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:42.360
Recreated data of a Neo-Baroque
style room, made on Mars.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:43.880
How'd you like it?

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:45.620
I have great taste, right?

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.080
It was pretty pricey.

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:53.360
Mademoiselle, please sit down right here.

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:55.360
Even your avatars are I-machines.

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:57.960
You Evertancers really are insane.

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:02.420
I'd say following military orders without
a single question like you do

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:05.040
is far more insane, really.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:08.840
You sure know how to do a warm
welcome, robot puppet.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:10.380
Alright, let's stop here.

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:13.180
Soldier girl, I've got questions for you.

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:13.940
Go on.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:16.800
First of all, let's hear your affiliation.

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:20.840
Planetary Federation's 12th dispatched
fleet's space regiment,

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:25.860
8th reconnaissance-in-force company commander, first lieutenant Amanza Volchkova.

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:29.680
Such a pretty lady, and a
company commander?

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:31.140
Really, seriously.

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:33.840
Looks have nothing to do with being a soldier.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:35.580
No, it's a great thing you're so lovely!

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:37.980
Rick, sit down.

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:38.400
Eh?

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:40.400
Take your seat.

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:42.400
Ah, okay, okay.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:45.920
Lt. Amanza, why was our ship captured?

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:49.220
To retrieve the illegally extracted Orichalt.

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:50.780
Now look here, Lieutenant.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:52.260
I've been in the military myself.

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:55.160
That couldn't have been an
official military operation.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:57.160
Where did the orders come from?

00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:58.920
Do you think I know?

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:01.080
Karla, what do you say?

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:04.220
Body scan shows that her pupils are not contracted

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:07.100
and there are no obvious changes
in muscular action potential.

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:09.000
I don't think she's lying.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:12.020
So we won't get anywhere by talking to her then.

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:13.180
Just a waste of time.

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:14.840
I have a question too.

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:18.260
I'm sorry, but do you understand your position?

00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:20.520
I know what you want to find out.

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:22.360
My name is Rick Ayer.

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:26.880
With three consecutive victories at
Asteroid Speed, Prince of Speed-

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:31.020
Were you the ones who unleashed
those meteoroids on our ship?

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:32.840
Of course not.

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:35.080
That couldn't have been a natural phenomenon.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:36.160
Obviously.

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:40.900
It had pin-point precision, and besides,
meteoroids don't Miguel Jump!

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:43.020
I don't get it either!

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:45.360
But it was obviously done on purpose.

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:49.520
And nobody but you people could've caused that.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:50.360
What does she mean?

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:53.560
She means there's a chance
they could come flying again.

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:55.280
Wait, why?

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:56.720
We didn't do any-

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:58.580
Wait, could it be?

00:09:58.580 --> 00:09:59.080
Rick!

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:00.880
Hey, look.

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:01.240
Eh?

00:10:02.780 --> 00:10:04.480
Is the data correct?

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:08.300
That bitch!

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:19.720
If it's a mining ship, there should be
cargo transport systems somewhere.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:21.660
Lieutenant Amanza Volchkova.

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:24.120
Let me tell you one interesting thing!

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:26.120
Hey, you listening?

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:30.180
This ship is outside the Miguel Net right now!

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:33.680
You won't be able to just jump out
and merrily be on your way!

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:38.080
Don't go away on your own.

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:41.020
You came at a good time.

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:46.400
I don't like this kind of stuff, really.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:07.220
Is that info about one of the new
planet's satellites warping true?

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:09.820
Yes, it's truth.

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:12.840
We just got an image from the probe.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:15.220
What could it mean?

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:18.520
Looks like we were mistaken.

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:22.660
The true form of Amatsu Mikaboshi
might've been this satellite.

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:26.860
We should consider there being
multiple of them too.

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:30.080
Did we collect too much Orichalt, I wonder.

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:32.920
The space sure is vast.

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:37.440
Let's assume the satellite is heading
towards the mining company's ship.

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:40.640
I'll inform the celestial body
observation and defense force HQ.

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:47.320
The lovely lieutenant took little lady and
the kid hostages and locked herself up?

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.440
What are we gonna do, Pops?

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:51.680
We do what we have to do.

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:53.200
And what is that exactly?

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:57.280
Um, I think you should really stop this.

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:00.780
Don't worry, if you stay quiet I won't harm you.

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:02.960
I'm not talking about that...

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:05.940
Bridge, I'll tell you my demands.

00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:08.120
Demands?!

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:13.080
Once the ship gets into an area where a Miguel
Jump is possible, set the course to Sevens.

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:15.200
We will also require food-

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:16.520
Nah.

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:18.520
No?

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:19.840
What are you saying?

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:20.300
The hostages-

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:22.260
Boil them, fry them, I don't care.

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:27.020
This ship isn't going to Sevens and you're
not getting any provisions either.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:29.640
If you don't want to die, surrender peacefully.

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:30.500
Over.

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:33.760
Knew it...

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:36.740
Pops, that's pretty crazy!

00:12:36.740 --> 00:12:38.940
That woman won't kill the hostages.

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:42.840
I'd like to think so too,
but how are you so sure?

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:46.900
That woman has never killed anyone
without being ordered to.

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:48.620
An imminent gravity wave!

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:51.020
Something's going to Miguel Out.

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:52.220
Again?

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:54.220
What are these numbers...

00:12:54.220 --> 00:12:56.540
This is strange, what's going on?

00:12:56.540 --> 00:12:57.740
It's coming out!

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:02.720
Doesn't look like the military,
or a civilian ship either.

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:05.000
Who is it then?

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:08.680
Who'd even warp into this place that's
not on the maps out of curiosity?

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:26.200
Gravity wave numbers rising! They keep going up!

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:26.800
Papa!

00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:30.180
Just how heavy is this thing going to be?

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:33.600
Is the thing that the lovely
lieutenant said going to happen?

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:36.000
In the worst case, probably.

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:39.800
Clair, send this image to the lieutenant as well.

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:40.320
Okay.

00:13:55.820 --> 00:13:56.800
This is...

00:13:56.800 --> 00:13:58.980
An M-1 scale Miguel Jump?

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:01.520
Wait, I think I've seen this before...

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:06.920
This is one of the two satellites
from that new planet!

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:07.500
What?

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:09.540
Why would it be here?

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:21.900
Papa, something just gushed out from the object!

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:25.340
There's a huge amount of it!

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:28.000
This spectrum, iron and nickel?

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:29.280
Just rocks?

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:30.840
This dispersion speed...

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:32.340
We won't be able to evade!

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:36.820
Is the torpedo we launched
out of the rocks' course?

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:40.080
It will be out of it in three minutes!

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:44.560
Alright, connect the Orichalt torpedo through
telemetry and perform an emergency jump!

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:47.140
We can't, they'll reach us before the jump!

00:14:47.140 --> 00:14:47.920
Shit!

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.600
Move out, all of you!

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:51.960
Clear away the asteroids on collision course!

00:14:51.960 --> 00:14:54.980
Minimize the damage to Stulti!

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:57.440
Making it sound so easy!

00:14:57.440 --> 00:15:00.400
Preparing to release Orichalt from
the containment device!

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:02.940
Entering the telemetry connection sequence!

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:05.840
You see how it is, lieutenant.

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:10.260
We need the girlie's astrogeology
expertise, hurry and let her out!

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:12.060
We need all of the help we can get here.

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:14.340
I'll allow you to use your I-machine.

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:16.920
Guide me to the MT room.

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:18.020
Okay.

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:20.240
I'll be controlling the guns.

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:22.200
Clair, focus on the jump sequence!

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:22.980
I got it!

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:25.140
Pops, how long do we have to hold out?

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:25.980
8 minutes.

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:27.840
Buy us at least 8 minutes.

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:29.360
"At least" 8 minutes?

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:30.820
That's rough.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:33.700
MT system launching.

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:43.160
So, where's the large-scale drilling rig?

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:44.960
Oh, the Mattsun?

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:46.720
In the 2nd hangar, I think.

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:49.980
Deploy shields and brace for meteoroids!

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:51.420
Don't slack off!

00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:53.700
This is outside the Miguel Net!

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:57.080
If we mess this up and get blown
off, we're never going to return!

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:57.880
Got it?

00:15:57.880 --> 00:15:58.680
Yes!

00:16:08.720 --> 00:16:11.340
Karla, how many are on the collision course?

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:16.940
There are 48 of those that exceed
our shield's durability.

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:18.940
Fourty eight?

00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:21.980
We've got 6 I-Machines here so that makes...

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:23.060
8 per person?

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:24.060
That's not happening!

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:25.760
We just need to take out three!

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:27.760
No, just two, actually.

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:29.760
What do you mean?

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:31.260
Like in billiards.

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:32.560
It's just physics.

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:34.060
Elaborate, please.

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:36.040
There's no need to break all of them.

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:39.440
Yeah, we just need them not to hit the Stulti.

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:42.780
So if we make them collide with each other in a chain reaction

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:45.820
and change the trajectory of the rocks
in our way, there's no problem!

00:16:45.820 --> 00:16:48.200
Orichalt torpedo, ready for release!

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:50.360
Fa-Loser, follow Maya.

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:53.100
I'll go with miss lieutenant here.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:57.440
Should we entrust this to a prisoner?
Maybe I should-

00:16:57.560 --> 00:17:01.580
My machine is more capable than yours.

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:03.260
Leave it to me.

00:17:03.260 --> 00:17:05.720
Don't worry, pretty girls can't be bad!

00:17:05.720 --> 00:17:07.120
Target approaching!

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:09.360
Explosion depth, 80 meters!

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:11.640
Mineshaft angle, 40 degrees!

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:12.460
Here we go.

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:17.720
Explosion timing, 300 seconds!

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:20.800
Start excavation!

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:22.800
Leave the defense to me!

00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:31.160
Explosion depth, reached!

00:17:32.240 --> 00:17:33.520
Fa-Loser, please.

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:38.120
Fa-Loser, let's escape.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:46.460
Eh? Mr. Ido's team is stuck in the bedrock?

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:48.860
Neither the drill nor Ido's kunai can
make a dent, they're saying.

00:17:48.860 --> 00:17:50.940
Looks like the hardness is over 2,0000.

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:57.860
There's not enough output.

00:17:57.860 --> 00:18:00.080
Lend me your energy pipe.

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:02.400
At maximum output I should
be able to break the bedrock.

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:05.740
Even if you break it, there's not going
to be enough energy to escape.

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:07.740
We'll get drawn into the explosion.

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:10.360
Just Trance Out and leave your machine here.

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:12.640
Look at the Evertrancer saying that.

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:15.980
Did you lose the worth of life
along with your body?

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:17.780
Shut up and hand it over.

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:20.740
That way the possibility that everybody
will be safe is the highest.

00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:23.240
Okay.

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:25.020
What's your name?

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:26.780
Ido, I thought I said it already.

00:18:26.780 --> 00:18:28.400
That's got to be an alias.

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:30.120
Tell me your real name.

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:31.540
I don't know it.

00:18:31.740 --> 00:18:32.580
Don't know?

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:34.140
I have no memories of it.

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:36.600
When I came to my senses,

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:38.980
inside the memory the thing called "myself",

00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:40.420
my ID

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:41.660
was 0.

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:43.340
ID-0.

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:45.240
That's why Ido, then.

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:46.000
Yeah.

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:48.480
Grayman thought that up.

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:50.740
I like it, though.

00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:56.840
Ido's team resumed the mining!

00:18:56.840 --> 00:18:58.840
Are they going to make it in time?

00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:01.420
Ours will start in two seconds!

00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:09.340
Ido's isn't moving yet!

00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:10.320
What do we do?

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:12.560
Mr. Ido, the detonation needs to be readjusted!

00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:14.560
There needs to be a precise angle correction.

00:19:14.740 --> 00:19:17.140
How about making the propulsion
come 90 seconds afterwards?

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:18.920
We won't know until we try.

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:21.100
Mr. Rick! Ms. Karla! I need to ask something.

00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:21.640
Huh?

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:22.800
Us?

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:26.060
What are you doing?

00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:28.260
Still haven't done a Mind Out?

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:29.780
What are you going to do?

00:19:29.780 --> 00:19:31.400
Struggle for my life, obviously.

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:34.540
I'll see your way of life until the end.

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:36.760
You're an evil person.

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:39.140
This might be bad.

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:42.060
They might not have enough time to escape.

00:19:54.760 --> 00:19:56.520
Mr. Ido!

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:00.240
Where are you grabbing?!

00:20:06.820 --> 00:20:07.980
Alright, Clair!

00:20:07.980 --> 00:20:11.160
As soon as Ido and the others
are in the field, jump!

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:11.700
Got it!

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:19.300
Why did you rescue me?

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:21.640
Because I was sure I would be able to.

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:26.620
Launching the collision chain and
picking the shortest route.

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:29.460
Only this girl could've done those calculations.

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:30.980
That girl, then.

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:32.780
Now I'm certain of it.

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:34.840
You're a bona fide idiot.

00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:36.500
Help me instead...

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:38.300
If you've got time to say that...

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:40.560
Stop this rotation please!

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:44.000
You really are terrible at handling I-machines.

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:47.640
Don't laugh, stop me...!

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:49.640
I'm going to throw up!

00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:51.460
I really will...

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:54.220
These guys really are strange.

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:58.860
Being alive really is great!

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:01.220
Just wonderful!

00:22:42.740 --> 00:22:45.270
Retrieving Orichalt used for the jump.

00:22:45.270 --> 00:22:47.390
Move the I-Machines to the third hangar.

00:22:50.440 --> 00:22:51.870
We're back!

00:22:52.900 --> 00:22:54.820
You've been here all this time?

00:22:54.820 --> 00:22:56.260
You weren't afraid?

00:22:58.070 --> 00:22:58.900
Um...

00:22:59.820 --> 00:23:00.910
What?

00:23:01.120 --> 00:23:04.120
Weren't we your hostages?

00:23:04.120 --> 00:23:05.550
Who cares at this point.

00:23:09.360 --> 00:23:11.680
For the ID data to not be anywhere...

00:23:11.680 --> 00:23:13.570
Is that even possible?

00:23:14.600 --> 00:23:19.940
Unless someone erased that
existence on purpose...

00:23:25.420 --> 00:23:26.740
Mikuri Maya.

00:23:26.740 --> 00:23:31.280
Incomplete abilities should be
compensated by experience or resolve.

00:23:31.280 --> 00:23:34.140
The fangs only she can find,
where are they now?

00:23:34.140 --> 00:23:38.990
The answer is in the undulation of metal
flickering in dim candlelight.
